  "reason": "The current best (config_025, acc=0.6352) uses pca_n2000 as the RNA encoder with imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, and weighted fusion. All prior multimodal experiments used pca_n2000, so the RNA encoder dimension remains unexplored in the best-performing regime. PCA is a linear dimensionality reduction; scvi_n200 is a nonlinear learned latent representation that may capture biologically relevant structure more effectively. Config_037 changes only the RNA encoder (pca_n2000 → scvi_n200) while holding all other parameters at their best-known values (vit_l, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile), making it a clean single-variable test. If scvi_n200 outperforms PCA, it opens a new optimization axis; if not, it confirms PCA sufficiency and the remaining budget can focus on other refinements. With only 2 experiments left, isolating the RNA encoder effect in the strongest configuration is the highest-information experiment."
}

